---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — PTCL Speed Test"
  description="Privacy policy for PTCL Speed Test: what data the speed test uses, what is stored in your browser, and what we never collect."
  canonical="/privacy-policy"
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy Policy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated: 21 November 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>
        PTCL Speed Test is designed to collect as little as possible. This page explains
        what happens to your data when you use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>The speed test</h2>
      <p>
        The speed test runs in your browser and exchanges test data with the nearest
        Cloudflare edge server to measure your connection. As with any internet request,
        Cloudflare can see your IP address while the test runs — that's inherent to how
        the internet works, and it's the same for every speed test site. We do not
        operate the test servers and do not receive your IP address or test results.
      </p>

      <h2>Test history (localStorage)</h2>
      <p>
        Your recent test results are stored in your own browser's local storage, so you
        can compare tests over time. This data never leaves your device. You can delete
        it at any time with the "Clear history" button on the test page, or by clearing
        your browser's site data.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts and no sign-up — we never ask for your name, email or phone number.</li>
        <li>No tracking cookies and no advertising trackers.</li>
        <li>Your speed test results are never sent to us or stored on our servers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Contact form</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form opens your own email app to send us a message. We receive only
        what you choose to write in that email.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to external sites such as ptcl.com.pk. Their privacy practices
        are their own; this policy covers only this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the "Last updated" date above will change with it. For
        questions about this policy, use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
